<title>FRANCE: Corsican tax office bombed, no one hurt.</title>
<headline>Corsican tax office bombed, no one hurt.</headline>
<dateline>AJACCIO, Corsica 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>A bomb exploded overnight inside a government tax office in the north Corsican town of Bastia, causing widespread damage but no casualties, police said on Friday.</p>
<p>No one claimed responsibility for the blast but Corsican separatists have carried out several hundred similar attacks in recent years against government buildings.</p>
